{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFollow-up (fix b) discovered during creatable-foldable-arthropods (fix a, merged as a0fc8d43556 / Gerrit 1761). Fix (a) stopped the runaway-loop guard from counting memo-served repeats as loop evidence. A second, independent defect remains in the completion verifier's evidence-banking path: at SEARCH EXHAUSTION, `BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE` banks `met=false` — i.e. \"the criterion is unmet\" — when what the run actually established is only \"the search budget ran out before sufficient evidence was found\". Banking a hard negative from an exhausted search misattributes absence-of-evidence as evidence-of-absence: subsequent verifier passes (and the close gate) treat the criterion as affirmatively failed, producing false FAIL verdicts on tickets whose evidence exists but was not reached within the window.\n\n## Proposed fix\nMake the banked evidence TRI-STATE: `met=true`, `met=false` (a positive refutation was actually found), and `insufficient_evidence` (search exhausted / budget hit / window truncated without a determination). At search exhaustion, `BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE` must bank `insufficient_evidence`, never `met=false`. Downstream consumers must distinguish the two — and there are TWO verdict-rendering seams, both of which currently coerce the banked value to a bool: `assemble_deterministic_verdict` (completion_banking.py:619-640, `met = bool(entry.get('met'))` + FAIL finding) and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` (completion_banking.py:705-714, backfills `met: bool(entry.get('met'))`). BOTH must render `insufficient_evidence` as an INDETERMINATE-style outcome, not FAIL. **Close-gate behavior (fail-closed):** an `insufficient_evidence` criterion still BLOCKS the close — the gate does not pass on missing evidence — but the refusal carries the INDETERMINATE remediation messaging (re-run verification, widen the search scope, or operator-attest the criterion) instead of asserting the criterion affirmatively FAILED. The behavioral change is honesty of the message and the recorded verdict class, not gate leniency.\n\n## Scope\n- The evidence-banking site(s) in the completion-verifier workflow where BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE is constructed at exhaustion.\n- The evidence schema + BOTH consumer seams that render per-criterion verdicts from banked evidence: `assemble_deterministic_verdict` and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` in src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py.\n- Tests: a search-exhaustion run banks insufficient_evidence (not met=false); a genuine refutation still banks met=false; verdict rendering distinguishes the two.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] At search exhaustion, banked fallback evidence is `insufficient_evidence`, not `met=false`; checked by a new unit test.\n- [ ] A genuine positive refutation still banks `met=false` and still yields FAIL; checked by a guard test.\n- [ ] BOTH rendering seams — `assemble_deterministic_verdict` and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` — render `insufficient_evidence` as indeterminate-with-remediation, not FAIL; checked per-seam by rendering tests.\n- [ ] The close gate still BLOCKS on an `insufficient_evidence` criterion (fail-closed) and its refusal message carries the INDETERMINATE remediation guidance, not a FAIL assertion; gate-behavior test.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.\n\n## Out of scope\nGuard/memo interaction (fix a, landed); verifier prompt changes; retry policy."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786726530472862001,"uuid":"a5e79e05-0a96-4c47-99de-39f711c8b377"}